  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post engine scales its output budget with the parsed input record count.\nThe budget is `max(100_000, 16 * records + 1_024)`, capped at `u32::MAX` with saturating arithmetic.\nA Tormach operation with 100,001 feed moves now posts whole and per operation.\nAn output refusal states the limit, attempted line count, and operation.\n\nThe emitter keeps a private counter.\nThe host preserves a refusal after a script catches the exception or resets its public counters.\nDirect output buffer writes use the same budget.\nThe output extraction helper moves into `js_host` to keep `js.rs` below 400 lines.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe runaway guard used a fixed 100,000-line cap for every input size.\nA valid operation could exceed this cap by itself.\nThe error gave no limit, count, or operation.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll eight pins in `post_output_budget` fail with the upstream implementation and pass with the fix:\n\n- `tormach_posts_over_100k_moves_in_a_whole_program`\n- `tormach_posts_over_100k_moves_per_operation`\n- `runaway_writers_report_limit_count_and_operation`\n- `caught_runaway_refusal_keeps_limit_count_and_operation_after_reset`\n- `large_input_still_refuses_a_runaway_script_at_its_scaled_limit`\n- `top_level_runaway_names_the_first_operation`\n- `runaway_in_the_second_operation_names_that_operation`\n- `resetting_public_output_counters_cannot_bypass_the_guard`\n\nThe initial unchanged-code run fails at the old guard and its incomplete diagnostics.\nThe mutation check restores all three upstream production files and makes all eight pins fail.\nRestoring the fix makes all eight pins pass.\n\nThe initial quick gate passed all 80 steps, including the sandbox tests and mapped downstream app suites.\nThe initial clippy run passed. The current-head results are below.\n\n### Review validation follow-up (2026-11-20)\n\nHead: `8ff39f5480e6acbffbbb2fbe038fbe1fc1e60cf1`.\nMerged upstream `main` at `f85163b0ca948250fd6a51360d14754a282e0340`.\nThis brings in the tracked baseline fix for #3050 from PR #3078.\nThe merge was clean. No hand resolution or new source change was needed.\nThe PR stays a draft for re-review.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed all 83 steps; 700 tests passed, with no failed or ignored tests.\n- All eight `post_output_budget` pins: all eight passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: passed all 200 selected steps in 24.9 minutes; 41 tests passed, six expected known failures, and no unexpected failures.\n- `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`: passed; all six `shared_face_bodies_finish` tests also passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: both steps passed. One light twin passed in 7.21 seconds; total time was 2.5 minutes.\n\nThe sole review finding requires validation and its record.\nNo new test or mutation applies to that finding.\nThe eight output-budget pins retain the RED then GREEN mutation evidence above.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe user's private `sc_logo.camproj` was not available.\nNo physical PathPilot controller, GUI posting flow, or MCP posting flow was exercised.\nThe pins use synthetic streams through the shared whole and numbered per-operation post engine.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found for the changed source, test, or decision files.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Scale the post output guard with the input so large Tormach programs post; name the limit, count, and operation on refusal.\n\nFixes #3002\n\n",
